1
00:00:05,904 --> 00:00:08,964
A warm house to protect me
from the wind and rain.

2
00:00:12,144 --> 00:00:14,574
And they gave me some fluffy warm bedding.

3
00:00:16,984 --> 00:00:19,214
Kompeito in the bottle.

4
00:00:20,384 --> 00:00:24,124
So what more can I ask for?

5
00:00:24,124 --> 00:00:26,884
I hope you're not completely
satisfied with one or two!

6
00:00:27,124 --> 00:00:30,324
At this rate, it's going to take you a
hundred years to fill the bottle.

7
00:00:30,894 --> 00:00:32,954
It's okay, Ioryogi-san!

8
00:00:33,094 --> 00:00:36,224
Even if it takes a hundred years,
Kobato is ready!

9
00:00:38,564 --> 00:00:40,904
Are you telling me to hang out with
you for one hundred years?!

10
00:00:47,644 --> 00:00:50,784
Kobato.

11
00:00:50,784 --> 00:00:53,614
Kobato.
Dou sureba iin dakke?

12
00:00:53,614 --> 00:00:58,014
Kobato.
Atarimae no kototte itsumo

13
00:00:58,924 --> 00:01:02,224
Muzukashii na

14
00:01:02,224 --> 00:01:04,994
Ureshii toki waratte

15
00:01:04,994 --> 00:01:09,294
Suki na toki ni utaitai dake

16
00:01:09,864 --> 00:01:12,304
Na no ni

17
00:01:13,604 --> 00:01:17,974
Itsuka negai wa kanau to

18
00:01:18,404 --> 00:01:21,674
Demo "itsuka" tte dore kurai?

19
00:01:21,674 --> 00:01:25,174
Machikirenai yo

20
00:01:25,314 --> 00:01:31,084
123! no aizu de ryoute hirogete

21
00:01:31,084 --> 00:01:36,294
Zenshin ni hikari wo atsumete

22
00:01:36,294 --> 00:01:39,124
Doko ni aru no?

23
00:01:39,124 --> 00:01:42,464
Oshiete, watashi ni dekiru koto

24
00:01:42,464 --> 00:01:45,304
Meippai kizu tsuite

25
00:01:45,304 --> 00:01:48,204
Seiippai hashitte

26
00:01:48,204 --> 00:01:52,174
Nan juu kai koronde naite

27
00:01:52,174 --> 00:01:55,214
Sore de mo mada

28
00:01:55,214 --> 00:01:59,234
Akireru kurai

29
00:01:59,714 --> 00:02:03,884
Ashita wo shinjiteru

30
00:02:13,564 --> 00:02:16,294
...Spring Green and the Flutter of the Heart.

31
00:02:16,294 --> 00:02:18,664
...Spring Green and the Flutter of the Heart.
You know what you have to do.

32
00:02:18,964 --> 00:02:23,494
Yes sir. I will heal broken hearts
and collect more kompeito.

33
00:02:27,044 --> 00:02:29,374
Little birds are singing.

34
00:02:32,044 --> 00:02:34,574
Flowers are sparkling in the morning dew.

35
00:02:36,714 --> 00:02:38,314
They smell great!

36
00:02:41,194 --> 00:02:45,284
Just wake up a little earlier in the morning,
and there are all these discoveries.

37
00:02:45,564 --> 00:02:47,754
Aren't you getting a little carried away
with this little walk you're having?

38
00:02:48,064 --> 00:02:49,864
It's not like that!

39
00:02:51,264 --> 00:02:54,034
Look! What a pretty little street!

40
00:03:15,454 --> 00:03:17,324
She's beautiful...

41
00:03:35,114 --> 00:03:36,704
Um, excuse me...

42
00:03:45,784 --> 00:03:47,414
I didn't think anyone was watching.

43
00:03:48,554 --> 00:03:50,954
Why are you crying?

44
00:03:56,364 --> 00:03:57,734
I wonder...

45
00:03:57,734 --> 00:03:58,894
Huh?

46
00:04:02,834 --> 00:04:05,964
Because the fresh leaves
are so pretty, perhaps?

47
00:04:07,114 --> 00:04:10,674
Do pretty fresh leaves make you cry?

48
00:04:11,884 --> 00:04:13,544
That's a hard one to understand.

49
00:04:13,684 --> 00:04:15,344
Sorry.

50
00:04:15,754 --> 00:04:16,924
By the way...

51
00:04:16,924 --> 00:04:18,474
Do I know you?

52
00:04:18,854 --> 00:04:21,414
My name is Kobato Hanato.

53
00:04:22,594 --> 00:04:23,824
I'm Kohaku.

54
00:04:24,324 --> 00:04:25,524
Kohaku?

55
00:04:26,364 --> 00:04:29,264
Ioryogi-san! You're a
stuffed toy, remember?

56
00:04:29,464 --> 00:04:31,934
Are you the Kohaku from Tenkai?

57
00:04:32,204 --> 00:04:33,494
Tenkai?

58
00:04:34,334 --> 00:04:35,864
Yes.

59
00:04:36,204 --> 00:04:39,194
That's why you don't seem quite human.

60
00:04:39,944 --> 00:04:41,134
Who is this?

61
00:04:41,344 --> 00:04:42,774
It's Ioryogi-san.

62
00:04:42,944 --> 00:04:44,704
It's all right with her.

63
00:04:44,944 --> 00:04:46,714
Is that true?

64
00:04:46,714 --> 00:04:50,044
Ioryogi-san... I've heard that name before.

65
00:04:50,524 --> 00:04:52,574
Ummmm...

66
00:04:53,854 --> 00:04:57,654
Hmmmm...

67
00:05:01,264 --> 00:05:02,564
I forget.

68
00:05:04,204 --> 00:05:07,654
Come on, don't you remember a guy with
a name that sounds like Ioryogi?!

69
00:05:08,504 --> 00:05:10,194
That sounds like Ioryogi?

70
00:05:12,304 --> 00:05:15,404
Would you happen to be the "Iorogi-san"?

71
00:05:16,174 --> 00:05:17,804
Yeah, you got it.

72
00:05:18,084 --> 00:05:21,054
What? You two know each other?

73
00:05:21,754 --> 00:05:24,014
Not much more than each other's name.

74
00:05:24,484 --> 00:05:28,684
I never would've imagined
Iorogi-san to be so cute.

75
00:05:29,024 --> 00:05:31,554
Well, as for this appearance...

76
00:05:31,624 --> 00:05:34,894
People know me as Ioryogi here.

77
00:05:35,064 --> 00:05:37,654
I understand, "Ioryogi-san".

78
00:05:38,504 --> 00:05:40,304
And you're Kobato?

79
00:05:40,304 --> 00:05:41,494
Yes!

80
00:05:42,504 --> 00:05:46,564
I'd better water the plants in the
yard before the sun gets too strong.

81
00:05:47,414 --> 00:05:48,444
So long!

82
00:05:48,444 --> 00:05:50,004
Yes!

83
00:06:09,434 --> 00:06:10,694
What are you doing?

84
00:06:11,134 --> 00:06:13,124
Oh, you scared me.

85
00:06:13,364 --> 00:06:15,234
I was looking at the leaves.

86
00:06:18,274 --> 00:06:21,504
No matter how much I look at them,
they don't make me cry.

87
00:06:21,674 --> 00:06:22,774
I wonder why.

88
00:06:22,774 --> 00:06:26,614
Beats me. When I look at these
leaves, my eyes water.

89
00:06:26,614 --> 00:06:28,284
Really? Your eyes water?

90
00:06:28,284 --> 00:06:30,014
Could you tell me why that happens?

91
00:06:30,324 --> 00:06:32,584
This person supposedly here to help is so lazy.

92
00:06:32,884 --> 00:06:37,164
So my eyes water just thinking that it's going
to take all day gathering these leaves.

93
00:06:37,164 --> 00:06:38,554
I'll do it!

94
00:06:38,624 --> 00:06:40,724
I'll be finished in no time!

95
00:06:43,534 --> 00:06:46,734
What a klutz. Here, let me help you.

96
00:06:47,104 --> 00:06:48,174
Kobato!

97
00:06:48,174 --> 00:06:49,604
I'll help, too!

98
00:06:49,704 --> 00:06:51,694
Thank you all!

99
00:07:00,454 --> 00:07:01,844
What are you doing?

100
00:07:02,014 --> 00:07:04,614
I'm trying to understand the
reason behind Kohaku's tears.

101
00:07:05,224 --> 00:07:07,884
If she's hurt, I'd like to offer some healing.

102
00:07:08,524 --> 00:07:11,554
I don't know how much good looking
at that is going to do to help you.

103
00:07:12,194 --> 00:07:15,824
But it might give me some sort of hint!

104
00:07:17,934 --> 00:07:19,664
I wasn't able to figure it out.

105
00:07:19,664 --> 00:07:20,964
I'm not surprised.

106
00:07:21,134 --> 00:07:25,404
Well then, I'll just have to get up early
tomorrow and go ask her again.

107
00:07:33,484 --> 00:07:36,014
I overslept!

108
00:07:36,014 --> 00:07:37,244
I knew this would happen.

109
00:07:41,324 --> 00:07:42,794
She's not here.

110
00:07:43,824 --> 00:07:45,054
Welcome home.

111
00:07:51,134 --> 00:07:53,034
It must have been a long night.

112
00:07:56,574 --> 00:07:58,434
It's Kohaku!

113
00:07:59,704 --> 00:08:00,864
Wait!

114
00:08:02,344 --> 00:08:03,544
Why?

115
00:08:03,544 --> 00:08:05,444
Don't be a nuisance.

116
00:08:05,614 --> 00:08:06,744
Nuisance?

117
00:08:07,014 --> 00:08:10,414
If you go out there right now,
you'll just be in their way!

118
00:08:11,684 --> 00:08:14,314
There was no need to come
out to greet me, Dear.

119
00:08:14,854 --> 00:08:16,484
You should have just waited for me at home.

120
00:08:16,924 --> 00:08:20,794
I enjoy walking home with
you like this, Shuichiro.

121
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:24,924
Besides, I want to spend every
minute I can by your side.

122
00:08:30,204 --> 00:08:32,264
My, my, what a lovely couple.

123
00:08:36,044 --> 00:08:37,884
It's a gorgeous mansion.

124
00:08:37,884 --> 00:08:40,004
Totally out of your league.

125
00:08:40,114 --> 00:08:42,014
Actually, you have no business here.

126
00:08:42,114 --> 00:08:46,684
I don't believe that. Even rich people
get their hearts broken.

127
00:08:47,354 --> 00:08:49,444
Where did you learn that?

128
00:08:49,554 --> 00:08:52,114
I studied the convenience store magazines!

129
00:08:55,864 --> 00:08:57,234
Ioryogi-san?

130
00:08:57,334 --> 00:08:58,664
Huh?

131
00:08:58,864 --> 00:09:01,804
When would be a good time to approach her?

132
00:09:01,874 --> 00:09:03,864
Uh no, you're not getting the point.

133
00:09:03,974 --> 00:09:06,404
Sorry I can't keep my promise today.

134
00:09:07,814 --> 00:09:10,604
That's all right. You were up all night.

135
00:09:11,114 --> 00:09:14,574
Besides, your patients matter more.

136
00:09:15,854 --> 00:09:17,284
You matter just as much.

137
00:09:22,424 --> 00:09:25,984
Kobato, like I said, there's no place
for you here. Let's go.

138
00:09:29,134 --> 00:09:30,324
Wha- Hey! No!

139
00:09:36,904 --> 00:09:38,774
Dear spirits in the water.

140
00:09:39,474 --> 00:09:41,104
Heed to my calling.

141
00:09:42,674 --> 00:09:44,944
Lend your strength to enrich the trees.

142
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:47,574
Come together to save their lives.

143
00:09:56,454 --> 00:09:59,014
Bring on the blessed rains. Pour!

144
00:10:04,604 --> 00:10:06,124
It's beautiful.

145
00:10:19,014 --> 00:10:20,484
Kobato?!

146
00:10:20,484 --> 00:10:21,884
Ioryogi-san?

147
00:10:23,284 --> 00:10:25,044
I'm soaking wet, you idiot!

148
00:10:25,184 --> 00:10:27,084
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

149
00:10:30,094 --> 00:10:31,694
I'm really truly sorry.

150
00:10:31,694 --> 00:10:35,724
No, we shouldn't have been
trespassing. I'm sorry.

151
00:10:36,764 --> 00:10:38,464
How did you find this place?

152
00:10:39,004 --> 00:10:40,624
Well actually...

153
00:10:42,034 --> 00:10:47,164
I saw you walking with a man yesterday, and...

154
00:10:48,174 --> 00:10:49,274
Huh?

155
00:10:49,274 --> 00:10:52,214
Sorry, I followed you!

156
00:10:52,914 --> 00:10:57,314
But I needed to find out why you were crying.

157
00:10:57,454 --> 00:10:59,014
I just couldn't understand.

158
00:11:00,754 --> 00:11:03,814
I mean, it has been on my mind and...

159
00:11:08,894 --> 00:11:11,734
Actually, I can't figure it out myself.

160
00:11:12,304 --> 00:11:14,864
It's just that whenever I see something beautiful,

161
00:11:15,904 --> 00:11:18,634
I think about how I would
love to show Shuichiro.

162
00:11:19,204 --> 00:11:21,144
I'm always reminded of him.

163
00:11:21,444 --> 00:11:22,774
I see.

164
00:11:23,614 --> 00:11:26,444
When I'm reminded of him...

165
00:11:27,654 --> 00:11:29,244
Reminded of him?

166
00:11:30,584 --> 00:11:34,714
There's like a "squeeze", and well,
around my heart I feel a throbbing...

167
00:11:35,394 --> 00:11:37,184
A "squeeze"?

168
00:11:37,624 --> 00:11:40,284
There's like a fuzzy feeling.

169
00:11:41,764 --> 00:11:46,134
All these memories start flowing, of the
satisfaction I feel when I'm by Shuichiro's side,

170
00:11:46,134 --> 00:11:50,124
or the occasional shy smile he shows me...

171
00:11:50,374 --> 00:11:56,364
it just all comes, you know, like...

172
00:11:57,074 --> 00:11:58,384
Like?

173
00:11:58,384 --> 00:11:59,874
Like...

174
00:12:00,014 --> 00:12:01,714
And then the tears come.

175
00:12:03,414 --> 00:12:04,784
I don't understand.

176
00:12:05,384 --> 00:12:08,914
Sorry I'm not able to explain it well.

177
00:12:09,154 --> 00:12:13,824
So what you're saying is when you fall in love
you feel melancholy and you get teary!

178
00:12:17,134 --> 00:12:18,534
Love?

179
00:12:19,564 --> 00:12:21,694
Oh I get it, it's love.

180
00:12:21,804 --> 00:12:24,204
Of course, it's love.

181
00:12:24,274 --> 00:12:25,834
You have no idea.

182
00:12:26,244 --> 00:12:29,044
I read in a magazine that
love comes with distress.

183
00:12:29,714 --> 00:12:32,904
Is there something that is troubling you?

184
00:12:33,814 --> 00:12:36,814
Hmmm... Well maybe...

185
00:12:36,814 --> 00:12:38,184
Yes?

186
00:12:38,484 --> 00:12:43,054
I wouldn't say it's really trouble,
but Shuichiro is always so busy,

187
00:12:43,054 --> 00:12:46,464
that we've never been out on
what you call a "date".

188
00:12:47,634 --> 00:12:48,794
Date?

189
00:12:48,994 --> 00:12:52,804
Oh apparently that's what they call
it when you go somewhere

190
00:12:52,804 --> 00:12:55,364
like an amusement park with the person you like.

191
00:12:57,874 --> 00:13:00,134
A date at the amusement park.

192
00:13:00,604 --> 00:13:02,634
Leave it to me, Kohaku!

193
00:13:03,144 --> 00:13:05,174
Kobato is ready!

194
00:13:20,494 --> 00:13:25,264
I can heal Kohaku's heart by having Shuichiro
take her to an amusement park on a date!

195
00:13:25,434 --> 00:13:27,924
First I'd better do some
research on amusement parks!

196
00:13:30,944 --> 00:13:33,304
So this is an amusement park!

197
00:13:33,704 --> 00:13:35,604
Looks like fun. Huh?

198
00:13:36,744 --> 00:13:37,174
Amusement Park Tickets
Adults 3,000 yen
(Children 1,500 yen)

199
00:13:37,174 --> 00:13:39,214
Amusement Park Tickets
Adults 3,000 yen
(Children 1,500 yen)
Three thousand yen for a ticket?!

200
00:13:39,214 --> 00:13:39,844
Amusement Park Tickets
Adults 3,000 yen
(Children 1,500 yen)

201
00:13:41,654 --> 00:13:44,114
Amusement parks cost money.

202
00:13:44,484 --> 00:13:46,474
But I don't have any money.

203
00:13:47,084 --> 00:13:48,924
What should I do?

204
00:13:49,154 --> 00:13:54,424
Don't ask me. Besides, I don't
think healing Kohaku is...

205
00:13:55,164 --> 00:13:56,394
Ioryogi-san!

206
00:13:57,934 --> 00:13:58,104
First Prize
A Vacation in Hawaii

207
00:13:58,104 --> 00:13:59,634
First Prize
A Vacation in Hawaii
First prize, a vacation in Hawaii!

208
00:13:59,634 --> 00:13:59,664
First prize, a vacation in Hawaii!

209
00:13:59,664 --> 00:13:59,734
Second Prize
A Vacation at a Hot Springs Resort
First prize, a vacation in Hawaii!

210
00:13:59,734 --> 00:13:59,934
Second Prize
A Vacation at a Hot Springs Resort

211
00:13:59,934 --> 00:14:01,504
Second Prize
A Vacation at a Hot Springs Resort
Second prize, a vacation at a hot springs resort!

212
00:14:01,504 --> 00:14:01,534
Second prize, a vacation at a hot springs resort!

213
00:14:01,534 --> 00:14:01,734
Third Prize
Tickets to an Amusement Park

214
00:14:01,734 --> 00:14:03,804
Third Prize
Tickets to an Amusement Park
Third prize, tickets to an amusement park!

215
00:14:04,474 --> 00:14:07,874
Spin the box, and the color of the ball that
comes out determines your prize.

216
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:14,474
All prizes are for two! Step on up,
try your luck at the lottery!

217
00:14:14,684 --> 00:14:19,714
This is amazing! Looks like they're giving
out amusement park tickets!

218
00:14:19,954 --> 00:14:21,254
Line up right here.

219
00:14:24,194 --> 00:14:26,024
Young lady, do you have a lottery ticket?

220
00:14:26,164 --> 00:14:27,394
Huh?

221
00:14:27,394 --> 00:14:29,834
You need a lottery ticket to spin the box.

222
00:14:30,234 --> 00:14:35,764
Oh? I need a lottery ticket before I can
get a ticket to the amusement park?

223
00:14:41,014 --> 00:14:42,444
Lottery ticket...

224
00:14:42,944 --> 00:14:49,444
W-Well, there's no sense in moping over it
forever. Besides, in Kohaku's case...

225
00:14:49,584 --> 00:14:50,984
Lottery ticket.

226
00:14:50,984 --> 00:14:53,074
I guess not too many people drop them.

227
00:14:53,284 --> 00:14:55,984
And here I thought you were all down
in the dumps about this thing!

228
00:14:56,094 --> 00:14:59,824
Now really. How can you even remotely expect a
lottery ticket to be just lying on the street?

229
00:14:59,824 --> 00:15:01,054
Woah!

230
00:15:06,404 --> 00:15:07,964
It's a lottery ticket!

231
00:15:18,344 --> 00:15:19,674
I have a lottery ticket!

232
00:15:19,844 --> 00:15:21,684
I'd like to spin the wheel!

233
00:15:21,914 --> 00:15:22,914
Here!

234
00:15:22,914 --> 00:15:24,474
G-go ahead...

235
00:15:25,184 --> 00:15:26,984
Here goes!

236
00:15:28,924 --> 00:15:30,854
Amusement park tickets...

237
00:15:34,194 --> 00:15:37,234
Congratulations! You are a winner!

238
00:15:37,234 --> 00:15:39,324
What?! I won?!

239
00:15:39,734 --> 00:15:40,894
Is this for real?

240
00:15:41,074 --> 00:15:42,104
Fifth prize!

241
00:15:42,104 --> 00:15:45,634
A stuffed toy alligator! Take good care of it now!

242
00:15:46,874 --> 00:15:49,844
Now that's just one more thing to carry around.

243
00:15:49,844 --> 00:15:51,404
Why didn't you say no?

244
00:15:51,684 --> 00:15:57,614
It's not nice to refuse someone when
they're kindly giving you something.

245
00:16:05,464 --> 00:16:06,724
But...

246
00:16:07,994 --> 00:16:10,834
It has to be an amusement park.

247
00:16:14,904 --> 00:16:16,594
I-I'm sorry!

248
00:16:17,174 --> 00:16:18,534
Fujimoto?

249
00:16:18,674 --> 00:16:21,374
Oh it's you! Pay attention while walking!

250
00:16:27,344 --> 00:16:29,644
You're delivering newspapers?

251
00:16:30,014 --> 00:16:31,154
Yeah.

252
00:16:31,154 --> 00:16:35,214
But Ms. Sayaka told me you
were working at a pizza place.

253
00:16:35,794 --> 00:16:37,784
I work at a pizza place, too.

254
00:16:38,464 --> 00:16:40,084
So many jobs.

255
00:16:41,934 --> 00:16:42,964
What's that?

256
00:16:42,964 --> 00:16:45,294
It's a toy alligator I got from spinning the wheel.

257
00:16:50,334 --> 00:16:53,534
But this alligator just won't do.

258
00:16:57,714 --> 00:16:59,684
Tickets to an amusement park.

259
00:17:00,214 --> 00:17:02,514
Those. They were given to me at work.

260
00:17:08,524 --> 00:17:09,584
Hey.

261
00:17:16,734 --> 00:17:18,394
What are you doing?

262
00:17:18,534 --> 00:17:21,234
May I have these tickets?

263
00:17:21,334 --> 00:17:23,274
Huh? Don't be ridiculous.

264
00:17:25,844 --> 00:17:29,644
Then won't you consider exchanging
these for Mr. Alligator?

265
00:17:30,444 --> 00:17:32,674
No. Why would I want that, anyway?

266
00:17:32,844 --> 00:17:34,284
Please!

267
00:17:34,884 --> 00:17:37,474
It's Kohaku's date at the amusement park!

268
00:17:52,734 --> 00:17:54,034
Here you are.

269
00:17:54,574 --> 00:17:57,364
Please use these on your date with Shuichiro.

270
00:17:59,204 --> 00:18:01,234
Do what you will...

271
00:18:01,544 --> 00:18:03,104
What's with those newspapers?

272
00:18:03,714 --> 00:18:07,734
Oh, they're letting me help deliver newspapers.

273
00:18:08,914 --> 00:18:12,974
You're delivering newspapers so that
you could get those tickets?

274
00:18:13,284 --> 00:18:15,274
Yes! So please.

275
00:18:16,194 --> 00:18:17,624
Thank you very much.

276
00:18:18,264 --> 00:18:20,754
But I really can't take them.

277
00:18:20,924 --> 00:18:23,324
Huh? Why not?

278
00:18:23,764 --> 00:18:25,994
Shuichiro is a very busy man.

279
00:18:26,364 --> 00:18:27,854
It would be impossible.

280
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:33,834
On the other hand, I wouldn't want to put the
tickets that you especially got for us to waste.

281
00:18:34,544 --> 00:18:37,014
I know. Why don't you go, Kobato?

282
00:18:37,014 --> 00:18:37,984
Huh?

283
00:18:37,984 --> 00:18:39,534
M-Me?!

284
00:18:39,744 --> 00:18:41,944
Yes, with Ioryogi-san.

285
00:18:42,184 --> 00:18:43,374
Huh?

286
00:18:44,654 --> 00:18:46,624
With Ioryogi-san?

287
00:18:50,024 --> 00:18:51,614
Stop imagining it!

288
00:18:52,994 --> 00:18:57,524
No! You must go with Shuichiro!
Otherwise it's meaningless!

289
00:18:59,134 --> 00:19:02,834
But... I really don't think it will be possible.

290
00:19:04,304 --> 00:19:08,864
Besides, I can't be asking favors.

291
00:19:10,114 --> 00:19:11,544
Would that...

292
00:19:13,784 --> 00:19:15,574
...be asking a favor?

293
00:19:18,354 --> 00:19:26,054
When I saw Shuichiro walking with you, Kohaku,
to me he seemed to look very happy.

294
00:19:28,394 --> 00:19:31,234
In the same way that you have
feelings for Shuichiro,

295
00:19:31,334 --> 00:19:35,564
I'm sure that he also sees you
as someone important to him.

296
00:19:36,334 --> 00:19:40,934
I'm sure he wants to go out
on a date with you, too.

297
00:19:41,514 --> 00:19:42,944
Kobato...

298
00:19:44,144 --> 00:19:45,714
Shuichiro.

299
00:19:45,714 --> 00:19:46,944
Huh?

300
00:19:49,284 --> 00:19:51,944
Is it really all right to have those tickets?

301
00:19:54,494 --> 00:19:55,984
Of course it is!

302
00:19:56,654 --> 00:19:58,184
Here! Please!

303
00:20:00,224 --> 00:20:04,524
Shuichiro. You don't mind going with me?

304
00:20:05,934 --> 00:20:07,954
I kind of like ferris wheels.

305
00:20:35,864 --> 00:20:37,524
Hm...

306
00:20:38,634 --> 00:20:41,174
I can't see Kohaku and Shuichiro.

307
00:20:41,174 --> 00:20:43,294
Of course not. Let's go.

308
00:20:43,674 --> 00:20:44,934
Okay...

309
00:20:50,614 --> 00:20:54,044
But I'm sure they're having fun.

310
00:20:54,414 --> 00:20:55,674
I'm sure they are.

311
00:21:04,964 --> 00:21:05,864
Ushagi-san?!

312
00:21:05,864 --> 00:21:06,924
What?

313
00:21:06,924 --> 00:21:08,594
A messenger from Tenkai.

314
00:21:08,664 --> 00:21:11,654
Tenkai? Another acquaintance of yours?

315
00:21:16,504 --> 00:21:18,134
What do you mean, time limit?

316
00:21:19,374 --> 00:21:20,734
By when?

317
00:21:23,974 --> 00:21:27,414
You're saying that the bottle must be
full before four seasons pass?

318
00:21:27,644 --> 00:21:28,804
Huh?

319
00:21:39,764 --> 00:21:41,194
You were listening, right?

320
00:21:41,194 --> 00:21:43,894
Yes. That there's a time limit.

321
00:21:44,564 --> 00:21:47,094
Four seasons, right?

322
00:21:47,464 --> 00:21:50,924
That means that you have
one year to fill the bottle.

323
00:21:51,344 --> 00:21:52,774
And if you don't?

324
00:21:53,944 --> 00:21:56,244
I cannot go to the place of my dreams.

325
00:21:56,414 --> 00:21:58,344
So? Any more in the bottle?

326
00:21:59,684 --> 00:22:01,274
No, the same as before.

327
00:22:01,454 --> 00:22:03,314
Any idea why?

328
00:22:04,214 --> 00:22:05,584
No sir.

329
00:22:06,284 --> 00:22:09,514
Wasn't I able to heal Kohaku's heart?

330
00:22:10,124 --> 00:22:13,324
You need to know that people
who are full of happiness

331
00:22:13,324 --> 00:22:15,764
basically don't need their hearts healed.

332
00:22:15,764 --> 00:22:18,104
Oh, so she wasn't hurt!

333
00:22:18,104 --> 00:22:19,764
What are you so happy about?!

334
00:22:22,404 --> 00:22:23,664
One hundred!

335
00:22:24,534 --> 00:22:26,164
What?! You're giving me one hundred points?

336
00:22:27,104 --> 00:22:28,044
Minus!

337
00:22:28,044 --> 00:22:31,244
Minus one hundred points?

338
00:22:31,544 --> 00:22:35,574
Wrong person! That's enough for
someone who can't get that right.

339
00:22:36,114 --> 00:22:39,814
But, but! It makes me feel
good that she was happy.

340
00:22:40,224 --> 00:22:41,724
You don't have time for that nonsense!

341
00:22:41,724 --> 00:22:43,124
You've got one year!

342
00:22:43,124 --> 00:22:44,494
It's time to get spankin' serious!

343
00:22:44,694 --> 00:22:47,524
Yes sir! Kobato is ready!

344
00:22:48,264 --> 00:22:50,934
Wipe that smirk off of your face!

345
00:22:50,934 --> 00:22:52,504
I don't have a smirk!

346
00:22:52,504 --> 00:22:54,104
I told you, I'm going to get
spankin' serious with you!

347
00:22:54,104 --> 00:22:56,274
Then what does a spankin' face look like?

348
00:22:56,274 --> 00:22:58,744
Like... don't be silly! Can't be done!

349
00:22:58,744 --> 00:23:00,434
No!

350
00:23:01,344 --> 00:23:08,974
Hito wa mina tonde mitai no ni

351
00:23:10,154 --> 00:23:16,254
Juuryoku ni damasareterunda

352
00:23:16,524 --> 00:23:24,364
Dare mo honto wa toberunda yo

353
00:23:26,604 --> 00:23:32,934
Ano ko ga anna ni kanashisou na no wa

354
00:23:33,974 --> 00:23:36,844
Jibun no kage wo

355
00:23:36,844 --> 00:23:43,974
Dokoka ni wasurete kichatta kara kamo

356
00:23:44,154 --> 00:23:46,674
Sore nara

357
00:23:46,854 --> 00:23:50,954
"Arigatou," tte kimi ni ietara

358
00:23:50,954 --> 00:23:54,834
"Arigatou," tte kimi ga waraeba

359
00:23:54,834 --> 00:24:02,164
Ittari kitari ureshiku naru

360
00:24:02,704 --> 00:24:06,934
Kimi ga shiawase ni naru

361
00:24:07,244 --> 00:24:11,484
Shinpai nante iranai yo

362
00:24:11,484 --> 00:24:15,574
Issho ni iru kara

363
00:24:17,354 --> 00:24:23,294
Ureshikuttemo namida ga deru nante

364
00:24:23,294 --> 00:24:25,994
Fushigi da

365
00:24:25,994 --> 00:24:29,034
Next episode
...Firefly Promise.
Fushigi da

366
00:24:29,034 --> 00:24:30,754
Next episode
...Firefly Promise.

